  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Cardboard Cowboy01** (2 reviews): Reviewer especially likes the two Cardboard Cowboy tracks on this tape; Phil's Cardboard Cowboy is among the pieces being worked through in rehearsal [2][3]\n- **Viola Lee Blues03** (1 other source): Take three includes harmonica and is aborted [1]\n- **Viola Lee Blues04** (1 other source): Take four features organ on verse one and harmonica, and is aborted [1]\n- **Viola Lee Blues07** (1 other source): Take seven runs through verses one, two and three, followed by short takes on the last verse [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Talk Tunings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Viola Lee Blues01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Viola Lee Blues02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Talk Tunings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Viola Lee Blues03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Talk Tunings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Viola Lee Blues04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Talk Tunings**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1966-02-05.136661.sbd.bruno.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 20 songs; 52 min; rated 2.25/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Sounds noise-reduced and muffled next to the near-identical Viola Lee Blues rehearsal tape, source 18846 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Bear ran sound at the Questing Beast and went with the band to Los Angeles soon after [3]\n- Tape works as fly-on-the-wall rehearsal, with the band working through Viola Lee Blues and Phil's Cardboard Cowboy [3]\n- Nearly identical to the undated 1966 Viola Lee Blues Rehearsals circulating as source 18846, credited to Uli Teute and Hanno Bunjes [2]\n- Reviewer thinks this material may have been attributed to a different date elsewhere [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1966-02-05.136661.sbd.bruno.flac16**: taped by Anonomous; transferred by BRUNO; source: Soundboard Master-Reel > DAT (48 kHz) [1]",
